---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy, Unknown Sender"
  description="How Unknown Sender collects, uses and protects your personal data."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <article class="page">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="updated">Last updated: August 2026</div>

      <section>
        <p>This policy explains how Unknown Sender (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) collects,
          uses and protects personal information when you use this website or book a game. We comply
          with the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>Unknown Sender is operated by <strong>Treadwell21</strong>, a company registered
          in England and Wales (company number <strong>16996311</strong>), with registered
          address at 71&ndash;75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London, WC2H 9JQ, United Kingdom.</p>
        <p>Treadwell21 is the data controller for the personal information collected through
          this website and the Unknown Sender app. For any privacy-related questions, contact
          <a href="mailto:hello@unknownsender.co.uk">hello@unknownsender.co.uk</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Email address (waitlist signup, booking confirmation)</li>
          <li>Team name (part of your booking, may appear on the public leaderboard)</li>
          <li>Payment information, processed securely by Stripe. We never see or store your card number.</li>
          <li>Limited technical information from your device (analytics, if you&rsquo;ve consented)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To fulfil your booking and deliver the experience</li>
          <li>To send booking confirmations and safety information</li>
          <li>To display leaderboards for the games you&rsquo;ve played (team name only)</li>
          <li>To process payments through Stripe</li>
          <li>To let you know about new games and cities (waitlist only, with consent)</li>
          <li>To meet legal and accounting obligations</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Stripe (payment processing)</li>
          <li>Brevo (email delivery)</li>
          <li>Supabase (database hosting)</li>
          <li>Cloudflare (site hosting)</li>
          <li>Google Analytics and Google Ads (only if you&rsquo;ve given marketing consent)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell your personal data.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>Waitlist emails are retained until you unsubscribe. Booking records are retained for
          the period required by UK tax and accounting law (currently six years). Leaderboard scores
          are retained indefinitely as part of the public game record; team names are pseudonymous.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to access, correct, delete or export your data, and to
          object to certain processing. Email <a href="mailto:hello@unknownsender.co.uk">hello@unknownsender.co.uk</a>
          to exercise any of these rights. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner&rsquo;s
          Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>We use cookies in three categories: <strong>Necessary</strong> (always on), <strong>Analytics</strong>
          (Google Analytics 4, only if accepted) and <strong>Marketing</strong> (Google Ads and similar, only if
          accepted). We use Google Tag Manager and Google Consent Mode v2 to ensure nothing non-essential fires
          before you consent. Change your preferences any time using <a href="#" data-cookie-prefs>Cookies</a>
          in the footer.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding: 80px 0; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); margin: 12px 0 12px; }
  .updated { color: var(--ink-dim); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  section { margin-bottom: 32px; }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--ink-dim); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 16px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  p { margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 15.5px; }
  a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
